      "## 29/08/2026 17:51 — Rajapalayam Murder\n\nPartner, **yes — the WhatsApp/Instagram poster you received appears to refer to the same killing reported today (29 August 2026)**. I checked the current reports rather than relying only on the poster.\n\nThe confirmed information so far is that **Thanikachalam (தணிகாசலம்), 46, from Othakadai near Madurai**, described in reports as a **former/Hindu Munnani functionary**, was attacked at or near **Rajapalayam Old Bus Stand** around midnight. Thanthi TV says unidentified persons stabbed him and fled, and police are investigating the motive. citeturn0search0turn0view0\n\nAnother report gives additional detail: he was reportedly a **two-wheeler mechanic**, had gone to **Tirunelveli for a relative's bereavement/funeral-related event**, and was travelling back toward Madurai. It says he got down at Rajapalayam Old Bus Stand at around midnight, where unidentified people arriving on a two-wheeler attacked him with sharp weapons. He was taken by 108 ambulance to Rajapalayam Government Hospital but died despite treatment. Police are reportedly examining CCTV footage and investigating **why he got down at Rajapalayam when he was travelling toward Madurai, who attacked him, and whether previous enmity was involved**. citeturn0search1turn0search2\n\n### Important distinction about the poster\n\nThe poster makes a much stronger political claim:\n\n> **\"நள்ளிரவு படுகொலை! படுகொலைக்கு கடும் கண்டனம்!\"**\n\nand calls on the Tamil Nadu government to protect people from \"social enemies.\"\n\n**The murder itself is confirmed. The motive is not yet established in the reports I can verify.** Thanthi TV explicitly says police are investigating the reason for the killing. So at **17:51 today**, it would be premature to conclude from the poster alone that this was a politically/religiously motivated killing. citeturn0view0\n\nurlThanthi TV report you sentturn0view0\n\nYour second link is a **The Hindu report specifically titled \"Hindu Munnani functionary murdered by gang at Rajapalayam bus stand\"**, but its article page is currently blocking retrieval from my side, so I won't invent details from behind that restriction.\n\nIf you want, I can **dig much deeper now across Tamil and English reports, police statements and political reactions** and reconstruct exactly **what happened, timeline, why he was in Rajapalayam, possible motive, arrests/suspects, and whether the poster's claims are supported by evidence**.\n\nI can also keep checking this case and alert you when police identify the suspects or motive.\n\ngenui{\"suggest_automation\":{\"label\":\"Track Rajapalayam murder investigation\"}}"
     ]
